  "text": "Rina opened the sacks. The flour was dry. Sol packed his tools and returned to his workshop, leaving Pip beside the mixing bowl.\n\nSol had brought his tools and a ladder. He was looking up at the roof. An intact spare tile rested on a shelf beside the bakery.\n\nSmall pieces and large pieces do not bake at the same speed. When the loaves are similar sizes, they can all be ready together.\n\nYou steer the seed boat. Drag the boat toward open water or use the arrow keys. Go around the rock to Grandma’s blue landing.\n\nSol read his unfinished draft. The others listened to the page he had brought, and its ending stayed open for him to work on.\n\nThe dough has rested and risen. Decide how to prepare it for the oven. Rina explained why similar-sized loaves bake evenly.\n\nPip’s flower will show Mara telling her story to Pip, Sol and Grandma. Place this picture in the lantern you grew together.\n\nTap it for its meaning and sound. With a keyboard, Tab to the paragraph, then use the left and right arrows to find a word.\n\nGrandma holds her own story page with Mara, Pip and Sol at the garden bench. They have found a way to share stories again.\n\nYour suggested ending. These words have not been checked against Sol’s account. Sol will share the version you last chose.\n\nTell these moments in any order you like. Your storyboard is optional, and the adventure’s ending stays as you played it.\n\nThat’s where my page stops. I know what happened afterward, but I haven’t written that part. What would you like to hear?\n\nPip watches Rina hand Sol the loaf. “Thank you for fixing the roof,” she says. Sol finishes the last line of his draft.\n\nHelp and Pause stop travel and cancel unplaced tile previews. Rina waits with her loaf when Pip leaves the bakery path.",
